☆Transaction
 >@Transactional - Follows AOP internally
 Commit id all success rollback if any failure
>Propagations - Required(Default value and uses if parent transaction exists,REQUIRED_NEW(creates new transaction even parent exists), SUPPORT(If parent exists use it else, without transaction), NOT_SUPPORTED(If parent exists suspend parent, run current without transaction else run without ajy transaction),  MANDATORY(If parent is not Transactional use it else throw exception), NEVER(If parent is transactional throw exception else execute)
 >TransactionManager- Hibernate,Jdbc, Jpa etc..( provides getTransaction, commit and rollback methods)

☆Isolation
  >Lock types- Shared lock(Shared lock between 2 transactions. If shared locked aquired another query can aquire read but, not the write), Exclusive lock(If lock aquired by 1 transaction no other query can either read nor write)
 >Isolation problems- Dirty read(Reads uncommited data), Non-Repeatable read problem(Same transaction might returns tye different values upon repeated reads),
Phanthom read problem(If range of data's returned might be differ when same transaction again reads in the same range)
 > Types of Isolation- Read uncommited(Reads uncommited changes by another), Read commited(Read only commited changes by other transactions/Aquires read lock and releases as soon as read completes, Aquires exclusive lock for write and releases at the end of transaction), Repeatable Read(Aquires shared lock for read and holds till the end of transaction, Aquires Exclusive lock for write and holds till the end of transaction), Serializable(Holds shared lock for range of transactions till the end so that no transaction can write  in the ranges)


☆@Async - Annotation used to execute a particular method asynchronously. To enable async in spring boot we need to mark SpringBootApplication class with @EnableAsync annotation.
- How threads created?
When this annotation is used Spring will loom for any default ThreadPoolTaskExecutor(Internally uses java ThreadPoolExecutor) is provided if provided it'll use the default one else it'll create pool for SimpleAsyncTaskExecutor.
- If we create ThreadPoolExecutor(Java) springboot will not auto pick it as deafult executor instead it'll go with SimpleAsyncTaskExecutor so explicitly we have to provide threadpoolname in @Async annotation to pick default executor. Or we can implement the AsyncConfigurer to Configuration classes and provide implementation to getAsyncExecutor method so this will be considered as deafult executor

